      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fish are the gill-bearing aquatic craniate animals that lack limbs with digits. Most fish are ectothermic (\"cold-blooded\"), allowing their body temperatures to vary as ambient temperatures change, though some of the large active swimmers like white shark and tuna can hold a higher core temperature."
      }
    ],
