        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Enzyme supplements that are activated in the digestive system of an animal after ingestion. Enzymes that are involved in the pre-treatment of raw feed materials (which aims to enhance nutrient availability and digestibility before consumption by animals) should not be classified as supplements as they are a form of biological feed processing."
