    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Components of a basal diet fully or partially substituted for non-woody crops grown primarily to feed to animals (e.g., alfafa or clover grown to feed to cattle) or non-woody plants harvested from non-cropped areas (e.g., forage grasses such as napier grass grown to stabilize terraces, cactus harvested from boundary fences, wild growing plants in wayside or fallows, algae, etc.). Feeds are added compared to a base practice control such as hay ad libitum only."
      }
    ],
