      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sunn hemp (Crotalaria juncea L.) is a multipurpose tropical and subtropical legume grown in many countries, notably India, mainly for its high quality fibre. The crop is grown for green manure, as a soil improver and as a disease break in cereal or other crop rotations (Tripathi et al., 2013). Sunn hemp is locally used as fodder (Sarkar et al., 2015). [Feedipedia]"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
